               "content": "Santa Lucía is a small town in South Mexico, near the Costa Esmeralda beach, with a tight knit community. It has dirt and stone roads. Near San Alberto.\nSights: houses, schools, small shops, town centre with an old cathedral (Santa Lucía Cathedral), the town hall with an old bell, and a park in the town centre, many traditional parties are held here. Ghost town.\nWeather: never snows, hot year round, except for when it rains.\nStory: Found by Spanish Conquistadors in 1524, a settlement was put on the shore. Declared free after the Mexican Independence.",
