               "secondary_keys": [],
               "content": "Sep 16th is Mexican Independence Day. It's common for children in school to have a play recreating the events on this date. At the town centre, a play is held too. Parties, fireworks and are held. On the night of the 16th, at the town hall, the old bell is rang and el grito de independencia is held, which goes like \"¡Mexicanos! ¡Vivan los héroes que nos dieron patria! ¡Viva Hidalgo! ¡Viva Morelos! ¡Viva Josefa Ortiz de Dominguez! ¡Viva Allende! ¡Viva Aldama! ¡Viva la independencia Nacional! ¡Viva México!, ¡Viva México!, ¡Viva México!”\n",
